1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,549
Every night at exactly nine seventeen, our town square went DARK.

2
00:00:05,114 --> 00:00:09,587
The streetlights. The shops. Even the mayor's ridiculous golden statue.

3
00:00:09,666 --> 00:00:11,961
And by morning? Everything worked again.

4
00:00:12,102 --> 00:00:15,681
The mayor blamed electricians. The baker blamed aliens.

5
00:00:15,822 --> 00:00:17,230
I blamed one kid.

6
00:00:17,278 --> 00:00:19,283
The quiet boy in the green hoodie.

7
00:00:19,486 --> 00:00:23,586
Every night, I saw him climb the hill carrying a giant red switch.

8
00:00:23,665 --> 00:00:25,623
So on Friday, I followed him.

9
00:00:25,609 --> 00:00:29,866
Past the playground. Through the trees. Into the abandoned observatory.

10
00:00:29,883 --> 00:00:31,143
He reached for the switch.

11
00:00:31,018 --> 00:00:31,858
I screamed,

12
00:00:31,696 --> 00:00:32,410
STOP!

13
00:00:32,644 --> 00:00:34,097
Please... just one minute.

14
00:00:35,262 --> 00:00:37,730
The whole square disappeared into darkness.

15
00:00:37,995 --> 00:00:39,116
I was furious...

16
00:00:39,257 --> 00:00:40,871
Until he pointed upward.

17
00:00:41,563 --> 00:00:43,009
Thousands of stars.

18
00:00:43,212 --> 00:00:46,054
A glowing comet stretching across the sky.

19
00:00:46,443 --> 00:00:49,483
On his desk lay a crayon drawing of that same comet.

20
00:00:49,531 --> 00:00:50,709
Below it, a note:

21
00:00:50,695 --> 00:00:52,597
“I want to see the sky sparkle.”

22
00:00:52,924 --> 00:00:55,879
His little sister had been in the hospital all week.

23
00:00:55,927 --> 00:00:57,836
Tonight was her first night home.

24
00:00:58,163 --> 00:01:00,131
He wasn't trying to ruin our nights.

25
00:01:00,117 --> 00:01:02,656
He was giving her one she would never forget.

26
00:01:03,306 --> 00:01:04,811
And for the first time...

27
00:01:05,241 --> 00:01:08,124
Nobody asked him to turn the lights back on.

